No — idle is stuck at 0 while waiting climbs steadily, which means clients are being checked out and never returned, not that 20 is too few.

The bug is in `withClient` (db.js:11-16): `client.release()` only runs if `fn(client)` succeeds. Any error thrown inside `fn` skips the release, leaking that connection permanently. Over an hour that leaks the whole pool down to 0 idle, matching the log exactly.

Fix:
```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```
Raising `max` would just delay the same exhaustion, not fix it.

