The cause is in `db.js`:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  const result = await fn(client);
  client.release();
  return result;
}
```

`client.release()` only runs if `fn(client)` resolves. If `fn` throws, the client is never released and is stuck outstanding forever. Wrap it in try/finally:

```js
